      "side": 1,
      "message": "Last time I checked, emscripten\u0027s version still used function pointer for `MapAsync`\u0027s callback. It didn\u0027t support lambda thus capturing variables weren\u0027t feasible. Not sure about now.\n\nWe should trigger emscripten trybots to verify. AFAIK they are not part of the default CQ dry run?",
