      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T06:46:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also FWIW, Greg mentioned that `prepareForReturnToCache` is not guaranteed to be called on playback thread all the time. If we want a more robust solution, I think we should register a mapping request and trigger them during playback.\n\ne.g.\n```\nbool DawnBuffer::prepareForReturnToCache(...) {\n\tqueueManager-\u003eenquePendingMap(this);\n}\n```\n\n```\nvoid DawnQueueManager::onSubmitToGpu() {\n    // This is guaranteed to be called on playback thread.\n\tfor (auto buffer: fPendingMapBuffer) {\n\t\tbuffer-\u003emap(); // or asyncMap();\n\t}\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "3f0d9821_00aa4941",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "e8bbd53e280e46138717bd5396841a559a123c2b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "328e0b53_7a2f8345",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 241,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T15:24:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We may have to do some work to get access to the list of buffers we want to map at the time we call submit, but could probably be done. Also is it safe to call \"map\" on the buffer while it is being submitted for GPU work? I guess as long as we don\u0027t ever actually try to use the returned mapped pointer until the GPU is done, it should be fine.\n\nAs Quyen said, prepareForReturnToCache isn\u0027t guaranteed to be called on the playback thread. The easiest example where it wouldn\u0027t is if Chrome starts holding onto Recordings for reuse, the Recording could be holding the last ref and thus we\u0027d call prepareForReturnToCache on the thread we delete the Recording. But in the current system and probably also true for the future, the vast majority of calls should happen on the playback thread when we see that a previous submit has finished on the GPU. So doing it in prepareForReturnToCache will give us the behavior we want 99% (maybe 100% today??) of the time and it may not have any noticeable impact for the 1% it doesn\u0027t",
      "parentUuid": "faa06c72_edcc9a74",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "e8bbd53e280e46138717bd5396841a559a123c2b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16140c7f_5f901d47",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 241,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T15:35:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Also is it safe to call \"map\" on the buffer while it is being submitted for GPU work?\n\nThe buffer is this list was returned to the cache via `prepareForReturnToCache` which means we don\u0027t use the buffer in any GPU submission at this point. Also based on my understanding of `prepareForReturnToCache`: if we call `takeRef`, the buffer won\u0027t return to the cache immediately. Instead only after the last ref is released in the map\u0027s callback then the resource will return to the cache for good. Only after this then we can start using the buffer?\n\n\u003e So doing it in prepareForReturnToCache will give us the behavior we want 99% (maybe 100% today??) of the time and it may not have any noticeable impact for the 1% it doesn\u0027t\n\nWith the current limitation of the Dawn/GLES, even 1% calls outside playback thread would trigger errors in Dawn/GLES because `glMapBuffer` would be called on an invalid thread. That would lead to undefined behaviors? crashes (writing to nullptr) or Dawn\u0027s errors report -\u003e GPU process restarts.",
      "parentUuid": "328e0b53_7a2f8345",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "e8bbd53e280e46138717bd5396841a559a123c2b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27963857_944004e3",
