      "writtenOn": "2025-12-05T14:49:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are some good points raised here. Perhaps we should get together in another forum to discuss them rather than trying to resolve this issue in a code review thread.\n\nI will argue that (unless I\u0027ve screwed something up) this change is harmless to land. It does not affect any running code. It simply makes available the same codepath that the Emscripten backend was already using to native code, hidden behind a Skia cap whose default value is unchanged.\n\nThe goal is to avoid shadow copies in Dawn/GLES for the most common cases: when an existing buffer is re-mapped for subsequent use. If there\u0027s another way of achieving the same goal, I\u0027m open to it.",
      "parentUuid": "9ed36ab6_b9d13b47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 34
      },
